  "body": "Direct-PR: operator decision 2026-11-06 on #368 (\"progress-model slide rework\", an exception to FREEZE 2 limited to this slide), tooling only, self-merged when CI is green and the adversarial review says APPROVE.\n\nThe problem: on the progress-model slide (#494) a lot being worked on showed as `macOS` or `ready`, and `macOS` counted every `host: mac` lot although the cloud now codes the App lots of M2.\n\nWhat changed (`tooling/roadmap/weekly/progress.py` only, plus tests and the re-rendered PNG):\n- new bucket `en cours`, right after `done`: a lot that is claimed (`G.CLAIMED`) or named by an open PR (`G.PRS`), whatever its host;\n- `macOS` keeps what only the Mac can do: a lot waiting on a capture, or a `host: mac` lot that is not an App lot of M2; a `host: mac` App lot of M2 goes to `ready` (rule of 2026-11-05);\n- captures moved from `human` to `macOS`; `human` keeps decisions, keys, settings, triage;\n- footnote, legend and donut sizes updated so the slide still fits 1920×1080.\n\nChoices to know: the stated order puts a lot claimed by a `mac/*` session in `en cours`, not in `macOS`; the Mac checks owed are not traceable per lot, the footnote says so.\n\nTests: `test_a_lot_counts_in_exactly_one_bucket_by_priority` rewritten for the new order (claimed, open PR, capture, M2 App rule, done outranks all); 40 roadmap tests pass.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CEBkjmFApUaMrewUvD)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Roadmap progress views now include a **Progress** category for claimed work and lots with an open PR, regardless of host.\n  * Host labels are interpreted according to the app lot type, including the M2 exception for `host: mac`.\n* **Improvements**\n  * Updated roadmap legends and notes to explain the bucket categories and PR fallback behavior.\n  * Adjusted roadmap slide layout and chart dimensions.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
